taxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-23T16:37:58Z","updated_at":"2025-12-23T16:37:58Z","body":"> @syntaxerror247 godot should publish that data, it would help prioritize bugs that are affecting the engine stability.\r\n\r\nYeah, having more eyes on those crashes may help, the android team once thought about creating github issues for some frequent crashes but never got to this, but IMO that doesn't really make sense since reports won't have reproduction steps (which are very important) and most crashes are only on low-powered devices. There's already some issues opened with crash details from play console but those are still unresolved as we don't really know the root cause. That said, the team is keeping an eye on them and is creating PRs where possible.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3687269027/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3690696364","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114196#issuecomment-3690696364","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114196","id":3690696364,"node_id